ginal": "The Modifyers Pilot.mp4", "mtime": "1760824657", "size": "19455", "md5": "8c4bd9e7d0101b341bb46ba4b22b19a6", "crc32": "53de55b1", "sha1": "db4c7a0f3e5691dd376f2c11029a21627dc3082d"}, {"name": "the-modifyers-pilot.thumbs/The Modifyers Pilot_000715.jpg", "source": "derivative", "format": "Thumbnail", "original": "The Modifyers Pilot.mp4", "mtime": "1760824658", "size": "66002", "md5": "07ba6847af7e7a17060ae6f483a90ea7", "crc32": "1ef17daf", "sha1": "04fa37fe8719d2cee4d849fbbd8afe639c89e6b4"}, {"name": "the-modifyers-pilot_archive.torrent", "source": "metadata", "btih": "76fd202bee0960534a92f1f3cef2602d4b4530cf", "mtime": "1760825034", "size": "5395", "md5": "1cd73020979e44956925c7a311602a03", "crc32": "4df88e29", "sha1": "74930918814664055f1947cfae97d0f09ea288a5", "format": "Archive BitTorrent"}, {"name": "the-modifyers-pilot_files.xml", "source": "original", "format": "Metadata", "md5": "c015c13f1a60872860f01794ed9f75b4", "summation": "md5"}, {"name": "the-modifyers-pilot_meta.sqlite", "source": "original", "mtime": "1760824587", "size": "28672", "md5": "32e84c896e712c9bb6ce9e61e011358c", "crc32": "244fc6fc", "sha1": "214a042a3dec7128a6e8199b5619cc220f9f742d", "format": "Metadata"}, {"name": "the-modifyers-pilot_meta.xml", "source": "original", "mtime": "1760824600", "size": "2920", "md5": "d57147556a6500663c82a7287dd1a8a4", "crc32": "81711220", "sha1": "dc1cfa42dc971eb058da16cd07d9ed10d2d7b4ef", "format": "Metadata"}], "files_count": 31, "item_last_updated": 1760825034, "item_size": 88278571, "metadata": {"identifier": "the-modifyers-pilot", "mediatype": "movies", "collection": "opensource_movies", "creator": "Chris Reccardi & Lynne Naylor", "date": "2007", "description": "The Modifyers is an animated short created by Chris Reccardi and Lynne Naylor. It was initially a pilot pitched to television giant Nickelodeon, but it was not picked up for a full series. The short features Agent Xero and her sidekick Mole attempting to thwart the efforts of Baron Vain and his legion of henchmen, such as Rat.<br /><br />The pilot was first shown on Nicktoons Network's Shorts in a Bunch series back in 2007.\u00a0<br /><br />The scene opens as Rat, one of Baron Vain's henchmen, is attempting to steal the All Seeing Eye from the Museum of Odd Stuff. After succeeding, but setting off the alarms in the process, Rat escapes to the sewers, only to be confronted by Lacey Shadows, another one of Baron Vain's henchmen. After a brief altercation, Lacey gets away with the All Seeing Eye and escapes to her airship in a rocket pod. However, Rat uses a grappling hook to stow away on the bottom of the pod.<br /><br />After entering a brief pattern of stupidity which activates the lights, Lacey Shadows is revealed to be Agent Xero, a superheroine who uses her powers to foil Baron Vain's plans. After speaking with Katz, Mole, Xero's sidekick, is ready to return the All Seeing Eye. However, Agent Xero insists that they ask it a question. Due to this insistence and a series of mishaps, Rat is able to get away with the Eye and bring it to Baron Vain's lair.\u00a0\u00a0<br /><br />The title is a pun on \"The Modifiers\", referring to Agent Xero's disguises.<br />It is obvious that the cartoon's genre is magical girl due to the way Agent Xero/Lacey Shadows transforms and her activation item is a diamond ring.<br />While there is no official source stating why the show was rejected, rumors suggest that this was due to being passed over in favor of The Mighty B!, a similarly retro-inspired, female-led series that was in development at the same time. Some others say it may have been too expensive for Nickelodeon's budget at the time.", "language": "eng", "scanner": "Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.7.0", "subject": ["The Modifyers", "Modifyers", "Chris Reccardi", "Lynne Naylor", "Nickeloden", "Cartoon", "Pilot"], "title": "The Modifyers", "uploader": "saturdaymorningrevivalseries@gmail.com", "publicdate": "2025-10-18 21:56:15", "addeddate": "2025-10-18 21:56:15", "curation": "[curator]validator@archive.org[/curator][date]20251018215640[/date][comment]checked for malware[/comment]"}, "server": "ia903100.us.archive.org", "uniq": 352387374, "workable_servers": ["ia903100.us.archive.org", "ia803100.us.archive.org"]}